import{_ as t,c as o,b as a,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BEqfOpL-.js";const n="/images/command_center.webp",g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Home","description":"Start here to see what needs attention and choose your next action. Home brings together your setup, LUCIA's current recommendation, recurring checks, and changes in your podcast's visibility.","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"features/command-center.md","filePath":"features/command-center.md"}`),i={name:"features/command-center.md"};function r(h,e,l,c,d,p){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="home" tabindex="-1">Home <a class="header-anchor" href="#home" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Home&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Start here to see what needs attention and choose your next action. Home brings together your setup, LUCIA&#39;s current recommendation, recurring checks, and changes in your podcast&#39;s visibility.</p><p><strong>To access:</strong> click <strong>Home</strong> at the top of the sidebar. Home is a single page without tabs: your podcast&#39;s name and cover stay at the top as you scroll, a status line sums up the day, and a <strong>Show details</strong> link jumps to the full show summary at the bottom of the page. Older guides called this page the Command Center; existing links still open it.</p><p><a href="/images/command_center.webp" title="Open screenshot at full size"><img src="'+n+'" alt="Home with LUCIA&#39;s priority, setup status, and next actions"></a></p><h2 id="start-with-lucia-s-priority" tabindex="-1">Start with LUCIA&#39;s priority <a class="header-anchor" href="#start-with-lucia-s-priority" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Start with LUCIA&#39;s priority&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When a recommendation is available, <strong>LUCIA&#39;s priority this week</strong> highlights a concrete action for your podcast. Choose <strong>Do it with LUCIA</strong> when available to work through the recommended action in <a href="/features/lucia-ai-assistant.html">LUCIA</a>. Other notes offer <strong>Open in LUCIA</strong> to review the context and next step.</p><p>Setup tasks and recurring checks remain available below. The priority helps you decide where to begin without treating every task as equally urgent.</p><h2 id="understand-your-optimization-setup" tabindex="-1">Understand your optimization setup <a class="header-anchor" href="#understand-your-optimization-setup" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Understand your optimization setup&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Your show is X% optimized</strong> card measures setup and optimization inputs. Below it, three tiles show:</p><ul><li><strong>Positioning</strong> — how many slots are filled across your six positioning sections. Open <a href="/features/positioning.html">Positioning</a> to add or review topics.</li><li><strong>Keyword strategy</strong> — your show keywords, which guide show-level titles and descriptions. Open <a href="/features/keyword-strategy.html">Strategy</a> to review them.</li><li><strong>Distribution</strong> — coverage across the main listening platforms. Open <a href="/features/distribution-health.html">Distribution</a> to check listings and feed health.</li></ul><p>Positioning completion and review freshness are different. <strong>Mark as still accurate</strong> confirms that you reviewed existing topics; it doesn&#39;t fill empty slots or raise completion by itself.</p><p>Optimization is an input measure. Your separate <strong>Visibility outcome</strong> describes how your show is performing in discovery.</p><h2 id="listening-analytics" tabindex="-1">Listening analytics <a class="header-anchor" href="#listening-analytics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Listening analytics&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Listening analytics</strong> card lists each listening source (your host, Apple Podcasts, Spotify, Amazon Music and YouTube) with its connection state and the next step for it, such as connecting an account or adding the owner email Apple needs. Open a connected source to read its reports in <a href="/features/analytics.html">Analytics</a>; see <a href="/features/analytics-connections.html">Connect your analytics</a> for setup.</p><h2 id="complete-foundation" tabindex="-1">Complete Foundation <a class="header-anchor" href="#complete-foundation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Complete Foundation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Expand <strong>Foundation</strong> to review the setup checklist and any credits you&#39;ve earned. Follow the steps shown for your podcast: they cover choosing or reviewing show keywords and competitors, checking platforms, and planning an episode. Your progress is shown as completed steps, with the next useful action linked directly.</p><p>Completed setup steps can earn credits for <a href="/features/social-publishing.html">Social</a>. The checklist shows which steps and rewards apply; completing setup does not publish anything.</p><h2 id="other-tasks-and-checks" tabindex="-1">Other tasks and checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#other-tasks-and-checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Other tasks and checks&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use this list for recurring keyword reviews, competitor checks, description improvements, and relevant YouTube actions. Open a task to reach the page where you can act. Tasks can change as your data and setup change.</p><p>If a YouTube title suggestion appears, it opens the relevant episode in <a href="/features/youtube-insights.html">Analytics → YouTube</a>. Apply the title yourself in YouTube Studio.</p><h2 id="get-your-show-seen" tabindex="-1">Get your show seen <a class="header-anchor" href="#get-your-show-seen" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Get your show seen&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Visibility outcome</strong> shows your relative position and recent movement. <strong>Open visibility progress</strong> leads to the <a href="/features/visibility-progress.html">score breakdown and timeline</a>.</p><p>The <strong>Social</strong> card offers a next action based on your progress: connect a channel, create clips, or publish a finished clip. Reconnect warnings need attention before you rely on scheduled posts.</p><h2 id="what-s-changing" tabindex="-1">What&#39;s changing <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-s-changing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What&#39;s changing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Review notable keyword movements and competitor opportunities here. After time away, the page can emphasize what changed since your last visit. Each insight links to the relevant evidence; a ranking movement alone does not prove what caused it.</p><h2 id="show-details" tabindex="-1">Show details <a class="header-anchor" href="#show-details" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Show details&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Show details</strong> section at the bottom of Home is the full summary of your show: Visibility Score, AI visibility, keyword positions, distribution, latest reviews, top charts and ratings. It loads when you scroll down to it, or when you click <strong>Show details</strong> under the status line. From here you can also share your rank with a <a href="/features/share-cards.html">share card</a>. See <a href="/features/podcast-details.html">Show details</a> for a widget-by-widget guide.</p><h2 id="move-from-setup-to-production" tabindex="-1">Move from setup to production <a class="header-anchor" href="#move-from-setup-to-production" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Move from setup to production&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The sidebar groups the next steps by what you want to do: <strong>Plan</strong>, <strong>Content</strong>, <strong>Get found</strong>, <strong>Promote</strong> and <strong>Measure</strong>.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Sidebar item</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Plan →</strong> <a href="/features/positioning.html">Positioning</a></td><td>Define and review who your show serves and what makes it different</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Content →</strong> <a href="/features/show-optimization.html">Show Optimization</a></td><td>Improve show title, author, description, and cover</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Content →</strong> <a href="/features/planner.html">Episode Planner</a></td><td>Plan and optimize individual episodes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Content →</strong> <a href="/features/pulse.html">Topics</a></td><td>Explore timely topics and supporting sources</td></tr></tbody></table><p>For an unpublished podcast, Home is called <strong>Design</strong>. See <a href="/getting-started/pre-launch-planning.html">Pre-launch Planning</a> for its rollout and launch-readiness flow. Agency teams can review multiple shows in the <a href="/features/agency-workspace.html">Agency workspace</a>.</p>',31)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
